### =============================================================================
### FleetPulse Driver API — HTTP contract for the mobile app
###
### Runnable with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.
### The mobile app is a client of the FleetPulse backend; this file is the
### single concrete reference for every request it makes. See PRD.md §5 for the
### full contract (including the WebSocket, which cannot run from an .http file).
### =============================================================================

### Base URL — point at your running backend (dev default below).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Register a new driver  (POST /driver/register)
###
### The account is created INACTIVE (active: false). It CANNOT log in until an
### admin approves it from the dispatch dashboard. Drivers are self-registering
### in V1, but gated by admin approval.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/driver/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Budi Santoso",
  "phone": "081234567890",
  "vehicle_plate": "B 1234 XY",
  "capacity_kg": 200,
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Expected responses:
### 201 { "message": "Registration successful. Your account is pending admin approval.",
###       "driver_id": 1 }
### 422 { "errors": { "<field>": ["<message>", ...] } }


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Log in → driver bearer token  (POST /driver/session)
###
### Works only AFTER an admin approves the driver. The token is what the app
### presents to open the WebSocket (section 3). Store it in secure storage.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/driver/session
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "081234567890",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

### Expected responses:
### 201 { "token": "...", "driver_id": 1, "expires_in": 604800 }   # 604800 s = 7 days
### 403 { "error": "pending_approval" }     # correct password, not yet approved → show a "waiting" screen
### 401 { "error": "invalid_credentials" }  # wrong password OR unknown phone (identical, no enumeration)
### 400 { "error": "phone and password are required" }

### Captured for reuse below (REST Client chains variables from named requests):
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}
@driverId = {{login.response.body.driver_id}}


### =============================================================================
### 3. WebSocket — telemetry & orders channel   (reference only, not runnable here)
###
### Connect:   ws://localhost:4000/driver/websocket?token={{token}}
### Join topic: "driver:<driver_id>"  (must equal the id inside the token)
###
### Phoenix Channel v2 wire protocol over the raw socket:
###   - message frame: [join_ref, ref, topic, event, payload]
###   - join with a "phx_join" frame; expect "phx_reply" status "ok"
###   - send a "phoenix"/"heartbeat" every ~30s or the server closes the socket
###   - correlate replies by "ref"
###
### On JOIN the server sets availability (busy if an order is in flight, else
### online) and pushes exactly ONE "active_order" event.
###
### --- App → server (channel push) --------------------------------------------
###   ping       { latitude, longitude, recorded_at (ISO8601), speed_kmh?, bearing_deg? }
###                → reply :ok | {error: invalid_telemetry | not_found}
###                bounds: lat -90..90, lng -180..180, speed_kmh >= 0, bearing_deg 0..<360
###   status     { status: "online" | "busy" | "offline" }
###                → reply :ok | {error: invalid_status}
###   pickup     { order_id }
###                → reply :ok | {error: forbidden | invalid_transition | not_found}
###   delivered  { order_id }
###                → reply :ok | {error: forbidden | invalid_transition | not_found}
###
### --- Server → app (channel push) ---------------------------------------------
###   active_order    { order: <order> | null }     # once, right after join
###   order_assigned  <order>                        # on a fresh dispatch
###   order_updated   <order>                        # on any server-side change (e.g. cancel)
###
### <order> = { id, status ("assigned"|"picked_up"|"delivered"|"cancelled"),
###             weight_kg,
###             pickup:  { latitude, longitude },
###             dropoff: { latitude, longitude },
###             assigned_at }
### =============================================================================


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### DEV shortcut — mint a token without registration/approval
###
### Before a driver is seeded & approved you can mint a token by hand and paste
### it into a dev-only config screen in the app. In an `iex -S mix` session on
### the backend:
###
###   iex> FleetPulseWeb.DriverToken.sign(1)   # 1 = an existing driver id
###
### Use the returned string as {{token}} in the WebSocket URL above.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
